      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the created_vcpus check does not guarantee that postponed_per_vm_setup() runs only once. Host KVM releases kvm-\u003elock before kvm_arch_vcpu_create(), so if vCPU creation hypercalls can run concurrently, those calls may observe the created_vcpus \u003d\u003d 0, execute the setup, and then successfully attach as separate vCPUs. \n\nBased on my limited understanding, I feel that this also makes the unconditional assignments unsafe. For example, a malicious host could set bus_lock_detection_enabled for one vCPU and a second invocation can reset it. I think this can have different vCPUs seeing different values for the global fields. Not sure if its a problem.\n\nCould we add a hypervisor specific boolean indicating that the per-VM setup has been completed, and test/set it while holding pkvm_vm-\u003elock in postponed_per_vm_setup? This state is distinct from created_vcpus: setup is latched before vCPU initialization, whereas created_vcpus counts successfully attached  vCPUs.",
      "fixSuggestions": [
