      "message": "\u003e Based on my limited understanding, I feel that this also makes the unconditional assignments unsafe. For example, a malicious host could set bus_lock_detection_enabled for one vCPU and a second invocation can reset it. I think this can have different vCPUs seeing different values for the global fields. Not sure if its a problem.\n\nI think this is indeed a problem, at least because in the following patches aosp/4151703 + aosp/4151704 I add bounds-checking `vcpu-\u003evcpu_id` against `kvm-\u003earch.max_vcpu_ids`. So if the host is able to change the `kvm-\u003earch.max_vcpu_ids` value via triggering `postponed_per_vm_setup()` second time for another vCPU, it can decrease this value, making the bounds check of `vcpu-\u003evcpu_id` done for the first vCPU ineffective (i.e. still allowing the out-of-bounds access addressed by aosp/4151704).",
